# 🚀 Terraform AWS Web Infrastructure

> Highly Available AWS Web Infrastructure deployed with Terraform — spanning multiple Availability Zones with automated EC2 setup and Application Load Balancing.

---

## 📌 Architecture Overview

```
Internet
   │
   ▼
Application Load Balancer (ALB)
   │              │
   ▼              ▼
EC2 - Server 1   EC2 - Server 2
(AZ-1, Nginx)    (AZ-2, Nginx)
```

Traffic enters through the **ALB**, which distributes requests across two EC2 instances in separate Availability Zones — ensuring **high availability and fault tolerance**.

---

## 🏗️ Infrastructure Components

### Networking
- Custom **VPC**
- 2 **Public Subnets** across separate Availability Zones
- **Internet Gateway**
- **Route Tables** and Associations

### Compute
- 2 **EC2 Instances** (Ubuntu)
- **Nginx** installed automatically via User Data scripts
- Portfolio-style web pages served per instance

### Load Balancing
- **Application Load Balancer (ALB)**
- **Target Group** with health checks
- **HTTP Listener** on Port 80

### Storage
- **Amazon S3 Bucket**

### Security
- Security Group with rules for:
  - SSH (Port 22)
  - HTTP (Port 80)
  - All Outbound Traffic

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```
terraform-aws-web-infrastructure/
├── main.tf          # Core infrastructure resources
├── provider.tf      # AWS provider configuration
├── variables.tf     # Input variables
├── userdata.sh      # Bootstrap script — Server 1
├── userdata1.sh     # Bootstrap script — Server 2
└── README.md
```

