## 🚀 Deployment Guide

### Prerequisites
- [Terraform](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/downloads) installed
- AWS CLI configured (`aws configure`)
- Valid AWS credentials with EC2/VPC/ALB/S3 permissions

---

### Step 1 — Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/CH-Nithin-Reddy/terraform-aws-web-infrastructure.git
cd terraform-aws-web-infrastructure
```

### Step 2 — Initialize Terraform

```bash
terraform init
```

### Step 3 — Validate Configuration

```bash
terraform validate
```

### Step 4 — Preview Changes

```bash
terraform plan
```

### Step 5 — Deploy Infrastructure

```bash
terraform apply
```

Type `yes` when prompted. Terraform will provision all AWS resources.

### Step 6 — Access the Application

After deployment, Terraform outputs the ALB DNS:

```
loadbalancerdns = http://myalb-123456789.us-east-1.elb.amazonaws.com
```

Open the URL in your browser. Refreshing the page will alternate between **Server 1** and **Server 2**, confirming load balancing is working.

---

## 🧹 Destroy Infrastructure

> ⚠️ Always destroy resources after testing to avoid unexpected AWS charges.

```bash
terraform destroy
```

Type `yes` when prompted.

